<title>FRANCE: French left election win would hit franc - survey.</title>
<headline>French left election win would hit franc - survey.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists were less pessimistic about the impact on financial markets of an opposition Socialist victory in a French May 25/June 1 parliamentary election than two weeks ago, according to a Reuters survey on Thursday.</p>
<p>If the ruling centre-right coalition lose, the median forecast for the franc against the mark in a survey of 15 economists was 3.40, compared with 3.41 in a similar Reuter survey conducted on May 7.</p>
<p>The mark was quoted at 3.3672/78 French francs late Thursday.</p>
<p>The forecast for the 10-year spread between French and German bond yields was also lower at 10 basis points compared with 20 in the previous survey.</p>
